    "background_story": "Pablo was a brilliant and reclusive mathematician who spent most of his life studying the intricacies of numbers. He was particularly fascinated by the concept of infinity and the vastness of large numbers. After years of tireless work, Pablo made a groundbreaking discovery - a formula that could accurately predict the occurrence of rare numerical events. His work culminated in the calculation of the billionth digit of pi, a feat that had stumped mathematicians for centuries. Pablo's achievement sent shockwaves through the academic community, earning him international recognition and accolades. Though he remained humble and low-key, his work opened up new avenues of research and inspired a new generation of mathematicians to explore the mysteries of the universe.",
